# Cryptography over bytes (D109). The sealed data and the password hash
# below were made by otterPS; both implementations must open them.
key is bytes from hex "000102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E0F101112131415161718191A1B1C1D1E1F"
fromOtterPs is bytes from base64 "AcwtHk4vfZKoGofXxF8xG9jeHgXhW34OiJFQ2HAxMNDjB5hwjLzeqD0+E6Pfr/g+MWlD67TmJlHbDNpCq706oHxPFaEKrTAaUxNH23hDGEm7"
decrypt fromOtterPs using key and call it opened
say text from bytes opened
storedByOtterPs is "otter-pbkdf2-sha256$600000$crmwxbM7qhtill0NUZ6Z+g==$XlKalIYebgl7PL/5G1xk4h85qHTqhtYEPQ8SMD9HAB0="
if password "correct horse" matches hash storedByOtterPs
    say "otterPS password hash verified"
.
if password "wrong horse" matches hash storedByOtterPs
    say "wrong"
otherwise
    say "wrong password refused"
.
data is bytes from text "abc"
say hex from bytes sha256 of data
say hex from bytes sha384 of data
say hex from bytes sha512 of data
signingKey is bytes from text "key"
say hex from bytes hmac sha256 of data using signingKey
say hex from bytes hmac SHA512 of data using signingKey
random is secure random bytes 32
say length of random
generate encryption key and call it newKey
say length of newKey
encrypt data using newKey and call it sealedAgain
decrypt sealedAgain using newKey and call it back
say text from bytes back
if data securely equals back
    say "round trip"
.
same is bytes from text "abd"
if data securely equals same
    say "wrong"
otherwise
    say "different secrets"
.
hash password "pw" and call it fresh
if password "pw" matches hash fresh
    say "fresh hash verified"
.
sha256 is "an ordinary name"
hmac is 3
securely is true
say sha256 hmac securely
attempts are
    0
.
for each attempt in attempts
    try
        x is secure random bytes 0
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        x is secure random bytes 2.5
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        x is sha256 of "text"
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        empty is empty bytes
        x is hmac sha256 of data using empty
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        encrypt data using signingKey and call it nope
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        decrypt data using key and call it nope
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        hash password "" and call it nope
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        if password "pw" matches hash "not a hash"
            say "wrong"
        .
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
    try
        if "a" securely equals "a"
            say "wrong"
        .
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
.
